From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMANET Firmware <noreply@openmanet.local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 23:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mac80211: accept duplicate ADDBA with hardware reordering

When hardware reorder offload is enabled, a successful RX BA session has its
valid bit and dialog token in mac80211 but deliberately has no tid_rx object.
The duplicate-token path treated that expected NULL pointer as a failed
session and replied with WLAN_STATUS_REQUEST_DECLINED. This prevents an
originator from recovering when the first successful ADDBA response is lost,
and is especially visible after a peer reconnect.

Return success for an otherwise matching duplicate when the valid session is
hardware-offloaded. Software reorder sessions keep the existing timeout check.
---

diff --git a/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/subsys/402-accept-duplicate-offloaded-addba.patch b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/subsys/402-accept-duplicate-offloaded-addba.patch
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/package/kernel/mac80211/patches/subsys/402-accept-duplicate-offloaded-addba.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+--- a/net/mac80211/agg-rx.c
++++ b/net/mac80211/agg-rx.c
+@@ -329,7 +329,12 @@
+ 			 */
+ 			rcu_read_lock();
+ 			tid_rx = rcu_dereference(sta->ampdu_mlme.tid_rx[tid]);
+-			if (tid_rx && tid_rx->timeout == timeout)
++			/* Hardware reorder offload has no tid_rx object. The valid
++			 * bit and matching token identify the active session.
++			 */
++			if ((ieee80211_hw_check(&local->hw,
++					       SUPPORTS_REORDERING_BUFFER) && !tid_rx) ||
++			    (tid_rx && tid_rx->timeout == timeout))
+ 				status = WLAN_STATUS_SUCCESS;
+ 			else
+ 				status = WLAN_STATUS_REQUEST_DECLINED;
-- 
